Package: gettoken
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}@DEPENDS@:gettoken
Description: token broker for AI agents
 An agent that holds a long-lived credential holds whatever authority that
 credential carries, and an agent can be talked into things by whatever it
 reads. gettoken hands an agent a token narrow enough for the job in front of
 it and nothing more, drawn from a super-token a human already holds.
 .
 This package contains the entry point the agent invokes and the privileged
 half that builds the request on its behalf. The agent never holds the
 super-token: it says what it wants, and gets back a token for that job.

Package: gettoken-token-requester
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}@DEPENDS@:gettoken-token-requester
Description: token broker for AI agents - the privileged half
 token-requester is what runs once the agent's ask has crossed over. It says who
 is asking and what they are doing from the kernel rather than from anything the
 agent can set, signs the request, and hands it to token-service.
 .
 It is not a name on a public PATH. An agent reaches it by invoking gettoken,
 which is the only public name the components claim, and never by naming this.
